course: dictionary
lesson: 11806
title: Beware: a warning word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Beware» is a warning. It tells you to be careful because something could hurt you or cause trouble. You will see it on signs and in stories. The sign «Beware of falling rocks» tells you to watch out before you walk under the cliff.
explain: Beware is a verb, and it is most often followed by «of» and then the danger, as in «Beware of the dog». Look at the words after it, because they name the thing to watch out for. Ask yourself: what is the warning about?
explain: Beware is a strong word. It means more than just «be careful»: it says there is a real chance of harm. Stories use it to build tension, and a sign uses it to keep people safe.
fact: Beware means to be careful of something because it could be dangerous or harmful.
fact: «Beware» is a warning word on signs and in stories, like «Beware of the dog».
fact: «Beware of falling rocks» warns you that rocks could fall on you.
fact: «Beware of scams» warns you to watch out for people who try to trick you out of money or information.
fact: «Buyer beware» is a saying that means when you buy something, you must check it carefully yourself.
exercise: «Beware of the dog» is written on the gate. What does the sign warn you about? | The gate is painted blue | The dog is asleep and quiet | *The dog could be dangerous | The gate is open for visitors
exercise: Which word is the warning word in «Beware of falling rocks»? | falling | *beware | of | rocks
exercise: Ellie reads a sign: «Beware of scams.» What should she do? | Ignore the sign because it is only a joke | Give her money to everyone who asks | Go and find the scammers to say hello | *Be careful and check before she gives away money or details
test: «Beware of the slippery floor.» What is the danger? | *A slippery floor could make you fall | The floor is made of wood | The floor is clean and dry | The floor is very warm
test: In a story, the old witch says, «Beware, young traveller!» What is she doing? | Saying goodbye forever | *Warning the traveller of danger | Asking the traveller for a cup of tea | Inviting the traveller to a party
exam: Which sentence is a warning? | «The wet paint dried quickly» | «I painted my bike blue» | *«Beware of the wet paint» | «The paint is red and bright»
